WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.155
An SRT file is a list of cues,

2
00:00:04.155 --> 00:00:06.431
each with a number, a timing line,

3
00:00:06.431 --> 00:00:08.241
and one or more lines of text.

4
00:00:08.650 --> 00:00:12.783
General Translation translates
only cue text and keeps numbers

5
00:00:12.783 --> 00:00:14.733
and timecodes unchanged.

6
00:00:16.150 --> 00:00:19.726
Then check line length and reading
speed against your platform's

7
00:00:19.726 --> 00:00:20.352
guide.

8
00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:25.305
Add an srt entry under
files in gt.config.json.

9
00:00:25.705 --> 00:00:31.475
Then npx gt translate reads
subtitles/en and writes Spanish

10
00:00:31.475 --> 00:00:32.693
and German files.

11
00:00:33.150 --> 00:00:36.528
Cue numbers and timing lines
stay exactly as in the source.

12
00:00:37.150 --> 00:00:39.773
Your team now ships
Spanish with each release.
